     <actual>
      <location ref="PS"></location>
      <dimension name="Age"></dimension>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The council is currently receiving complaints from customers as well as from SPs. So far, hundreds of phone calls ( mostly related to water shortages, reduced pressure, continuity or water bills), written complaints related to water system&#x2019;s needs, fairness in water distribution by the WBWD and allocations) or direct attendance to the council is being considered. However, this part of article 24 of the law, is not fully published and customers are not fully aware of this mandate issue. During year 1 of the program therefore, a complaints system was in place, but it was an informal and not structurally advertised system. For the coming program years, the complaints systems will be further formalized and made known to the public and SPs. To accomplish this, the WSRC is currently preparing an on-line complaints system. 
One of the reasons for developing an online system is to make sure that all complaints are registered and documented. Once this system is completed (August-September 2023) it will be widely published through:

-	Notification of all MOLG directorates
-	Council website and face book, local radios, 
-	Direct announcement within SPs workshops
-	The council will try to publish through PWA website.
-	An office will be named within the council to receive and respond to complaints.

This formalized complaint system will be operated, advertised and communicated by a new staff member of the WSRC who is already appointed and who will start work in July 2023. Altogether therefore, the WSRC is confident that the planning for this indicator will be met in the coming program years.</narrative>
      </comment>
